---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import Section from '../components/Section.astro'
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro'
---
<Base title={'Ommisa CLI'} description={'The Ommisa CLI runs the same assistant at the terminal: a thread that holds context, piped input, images on a question, machine-readable output, and a local log.'}>
<div class="page-narrow prose">
  <Hero title="Ommisa CLI" lede="The same assistant at the terminal — the reply is the only thing on standard output; the spinner, citations and warnings ride standard error, so redirection and pipes stay clean.">
  </Hero>

  <Section id="install" title="Installation">
    <CodeBlock title="requires Node.js 18+" code={`npm install -g @ommisa/cli
ommisa status`} />
    <p>The package carries no runtime dependencies. <code>ommisa status</code> reports the service, the signed-in account, and where the day's quota stands.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="signin" title="Signing in">
    <CodeBlock title="device flow — approve the code in the browser" code={`ommisa login
ommisa login --read-only
ommisa whoami
ommisa logout`} />
    <p>Sign-in runs the device flow: a code to approve in the browser, credentials stored under <code>~/.config/ommisa/credentials.json</code> (mode 0600). The default scope grants read and write; <code>--read-only</code> drops the write scope — storing conversations and memory files is then refused. Without credentials every command uses the public tier.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="asking" title="Asking questions">
    <CodeBlock code={`ommisa ask "What is the MPE requirement for a load cell per OIML R 60?"
ommisa ask --lang fr "Qu'est-ce que l'EMT d'une cellule de charge ?"
ommisa ask "..." --attach nameplate.png
cat report.md | ommisa ask "Summarize this against R 60."
ommisa ask "..." --save
ommisa ask -c "..."`} />
    <p>The tier, the remaining quota and the sign-in instruction print with every answer. <code>--fresh</code> bypasses the answer caches; <code>--save</code> stores the turn as a conversation; <code>--conversation &lt;id&gt;</code> continues a stored one and <code>-c</code> the most recent. <code>--attach</code> puts a PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF image (at most 4 MB) on the question — a photo is seen only in the turn it accompanies. Piped standard input becomes the question's context.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="chat" title="A thread in the terminal">
    <CodeBlock title="ommisa chat" code={`› What is the MPE for a class III load cell?
› and for class IIII?
/new      clears the thread
/attach FILE   puts an image on the next question
/lang fr answers in French from here on
/save     stores the thread to your account
/exit`} />
    <p>Every follow-up rides the thread's history. Markdown answers render for the terminal when standard output is a screen.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="composing" title="Composing with other tools">
    <CodeBlock code={`ommisa ask "..." --json         # the full response document on stdout
ommisa ask "..." --stream-json  # NDJSON events: stage, token, done
ommisa ask "..." -o answer.md   # the markdown reply to a file
ommisa log [N]                  # the last asks from this machine's log`} />
    <p>The <code>--json</code> option prints the machine-readable response — the answer, its citations, the measured confidence, the entailment support and the quota. The exit code is a contract: <strong>0</strong> for a delivered answer, <strong>1</strong> for a failure, <strong>2</strong> for a usage error, <strong>4</strong> for a spent quota, <strong>130</strong> for an interruption.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="memory" title="Memory files, conversations and projects">
    <CodeBlock code={`ommisa memories
ommisa memories add "Our lab" "We verify load cells to R 60."
ommisa conversations
ommisa conversations show <id>
ommisa files [project-id]`} />
    <p>Selected memory files join your asks as context. Conversations store threads across machines; projects bind conversations and files into one context in the web application.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="config" title="Configuration">
    <p>Environment overrides — <code>OMMISA_ID</code>, <code>OMMISA_API</code>, <code>OMMISA_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>OMMISA_SCOPE</code> — each also takes a flag. Every ask lands in the local log at <code>~/.config/ommisa/log.jsonl</code>; the log never leaves the machine.</p>
  </Section>
</div>
</Base>
